    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83430" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλά̆θᾰν-ον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dish</i> or <i>mould</i>
			in which bread, cakes, etc. were baked, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15.115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				70.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.22
			</span></i>, etc.: hence  the baking-woman in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
			</span></i> is called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλαθάνη</span>; cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλαθά, κοροπλάθος</span>.</div>
